// Memory-operation terms (include/sea/Expr/MemOps.hh, SeaMRules.hh rowMemOp;
// docs/design/SeaM-memops.md "Validation"): the read equations of mcopy /
// mset / mhavoc against a guarded-store expansion at 4-bit addresses (n = 0,
// maximal n, wraparound, overlap, memory versions, ites), one H per mhavoc,
// store-map interaction, the read rules with their premises, the boundary
// with the rules off or interrupted, and its refusal of unread terms; the
// PTR_INDEX operators (docs/design/PtrIndex.md) and their expansion.
RUN: sea-memops-test | FileCheck %s
REQUIRES: yices
CHECK-DAG: read-eq: mcopy ok
CHECK-DAG: read-eq: mcopy-overlap ok
CHECK-DAG: read-eq: mcopy-n0 ok
CHECK-DAG: read-eq: mcopy-nmax ok
CHECK-DAG: read-eq: mset ok
CHECK-DAG: read-eq: mhavoc ok
CHECK: test: read-equations ok
CHECK: test: havoc-one-array ok
CHECK: test: rules ok
CHECK: test: null ok
CHECK: test: prune-size0 ok
CHECK: test: wide ok
CHECK: test: wide-review ok
CHECK: test: wide-congruent ok
CHECK: test: wide-aligned ok
CHECK: test: wide-byte-in ok
CHECK: test: store-map ok
CHECK: test: boundary ok
CHECK: test: ptr-index ok
CHECK: failures: 0

// The log tag yices.const-array (docs/reference/logging.md): the assertion
// yices is about to refuse, not the rewritten one before it.
RUN: not --crash sea-memops-test const-array-log 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=LOG
LOG-NOT: log: yices.const-array
LOG: const-array-log: unsupported assertion next
LOG-NEXT: log: yices.const-array const-arrays=2 assertion="(const-array(bv(4), x)=const-array(bv(4), 0:bv(8)))"
LOG-NEXT: the context does not support lambda terms

